-
-The 2D canvas has been noised per container for a long time (canvas-spoofing
-.patch), but the WebGL readback paths were completely unprotected. Draw a
-scene, then either canvas.toDataURL()/toBlob() on the WebGL context or
-gl.readPixels(), and the result was byte-identical across containers AND
-across machines — the classic webglHash used by FingerprintJS and CreepJS.
-
-Verified before this patch: two containers with different canvas:seed produced
-identical readPixels (15e80087) and identical WebGL toDataURL (62625e96)
-hashes, while the 2D canvas beside them correctly differed.
-
-Two hooks, both reusing CanvasFingerprintManager::ApplyCanvasNoise with the
-same canvas:seed the 2D context uses, so all of a container's surfaces stay
-mutually consistent:
-
-  * GetImageBuffer  — the toDataURL / toBlob extraction path. Deliberately NOT
-    Gecko's own ImageExtraction::Randomize branch above it: that re-randomises
-    per call, which would break Cloakfox's same-container-same-fingerprint
-    invariant.
-
-  * DoReadPixels    — gl.readPixels, patched on both the in-process and the
-    IPC path so the two cannot diverge. Restricted to 8-bit RGBA: float and
-    integer formats are used for GPU compute readback, where perturbing values
-    corrupts results rather than defending a fingerprint.
